Guild Charter
<br />
Our Mission
<br />
Our purpose is to foster a community where having a good time is more important than the acquisition of items, wealth or power. To that end, we hold our mission to be first and foremost the amusement of ourselves and our companions be they guildmates or merely friends. Second only to that is helping those in need, be they guildmates or other. Having a good time should not (where possible) be at the expense of others unless you know the person in question to be of a good natured sort who can stand a good ribbing now and again, or of such a foul temper that you feel no amount of restraint or kindness would make any difference in their outlook.  In which case, put your best foot forward, and tease them as tactfully and mercilessly as you can. 
<br />
Guidelines and Beliefs
<br />
Part of the purpose of this guild is to help one another in this wonderful world of Norrath. As much as we would like to help in every situation sometimes a problem is best handled by someone else. Below are some guidelines to things we most definitely will, or most definitely will not help with. 
<br />

<br />

<br />
Guildwars: The Revellers will never be involved in a guild war that is not done entirely for role-play reasons.  
<br />

<br />
Killstealing: It is a fact of life that at some point or another, you will have your prey stolen out from under you. You can pretty much guarantee that sometimes, you will unwittingly steal from another. Honest mistakes happen all the time and a little patience and understanding go a long way. That being said, if someone is deliberately KSing you, please use / petition and/or /report and let SOE deal with them.
<br />

<br />
Powerleveling and Twinking: Although there are many strong beliefs about both of these practices, we believe it is a personal choice that each player makes in the development of their character. That being said, please do not ask on guild chat, or ever expect any other member of The Revellers to power level or twink you. This is not the purpose of the Revellers and no one in the guild owes any other members any items or exp by divine right. If someone is nice enough to help you, thank them graciously. 
<br />

<br />
Corpse Retrieval: Sometimes, you die in a very bad spot. It may be difficult or nearly impossible to get to your body without assistance. In such a case please ask on guild chat for assistance with the corpse retrieval of your body or of those of your companions.   If you are the recipient of such a plea, it is not required of you to help, but strongly encouraged that you do so if within your power.   
<br />

<br />
Quest Items and Armor and Equipment (Camping): An important part of a character's progression is the acquisition of new items and equipment raise one's level of effectiveness. Although it is wholly appropriate to ask for assistance or company on a camp or quest, it is not appropriate for you to ask someone to camp or quest for you. Especially if the item you're trying to get is far beyond what is possible for your character to attain normally. (For example, don't ask for assistance with completing your class quest armor or camping an SMR at lvl 5). 
<br />

<br />
NOTE: Although it is appropriate for you to ask for assistance, no one is required to assist you simply by virtue of your guild status or your level. A proven dedication to your guild and your character and a reputation for being friendly, helpful and gracious are all factors in the possibility of assistance on a guild level. All requests will be dealt with on an individual basis.
<br />

<br />

<br />
Acquisition of Gear:  The Revellers are a Need Before Greed guild.   In general, when guild hunts or raids are organized looting is handled utilizing a master looter with distribution as follows.   When a 'good' item drops all those who CAN and WILL use it will /random  (low roll wins).   If no member of the group/raid will use, it is offered up for rolling upon for group/raid attendees' alts.   If no one will use, it either goes to the guild bank for another guild member's use, or dropped on to a guild merchant to be sold and proceeds apportioned to those on that night's hunt; in rare instances it will instead be sold to finance guild needs (gems and coffins typically).   Tradeskill items are held for those within the guild who need.   All sellables are sold and split amongst those hunting, after component costs are met.   
<br />

<br />
Occasionally we will organize hunts whose purpose is to equip specific members of the guild (generally in the case of a server transfer)  -- in that instance, all items that they or their designated alts can use will be defaulted to them.   Remaining items will be handled as above.   Similarly, hunts may on occasion be organized to obtain a specific item for a specific person.   In that instance, said item will be defaulted.  All other items will be rolled on as above, excluding the person being raided for unless no one else will use.
<br />

<br />
Sale of items through the Guild: A person's personal property is their own to do with as they wish. The Revellers do not make any claim to your items, nor require any person to offer items to the guild first at discounted rates. That being said, if you can afford to do so please contribute items to the guild whenever you can.  If you can afford to sell them at a discount, that's wonderful. If you are affluent enough to be able to bestow it to someone that's great too! Your generosity has a way of getting back to you in unexpected ways and your guild leaders will take note of your past history of generosity when the time comes that you may need something from the guild. 
<br />

<br />
NOTE: Anyone caught buying or accepting guild items on discount or for free for the express purpose of reselling such items outside of the guild at a profit will be removed from the guild. Taking advantage of the kindness of others will not be tolerated.
<br />

<br />
Planes and Dragon Raids: The Revellers are a community, not an army. At this time, it is unlikely that we will be organizing dragon or planar raids on a regular basis.  It is possible that we will be invited to participate in those of friendly guilds, and we are investigating alliances which may result in alliance raids.   We also are of an age and size to organize small in-guild raids, on an infrequent basis.     Such raids are not mandatory, their purpose is to promote guild bonding and provide a challenge while having FUN.    If this interests you, volunteering to run a raid yourself is encouraged.
<br />

<br />

<br />
The Offer of Services to the Guild: Many characters have unique abilities (Resurrection, Teleportation, Trade skills (Smithing and Jeweling!), Commonly begged Buffs (SoW, Clarity, Invis), or class abilities (Corpse Location, Tracking). These unique qualities are valuable to the community and it would be appreciated if these were shared with the guild when possible. That being said, these abilities belong to the characters who have earned them, and often cost them mana, time and attention that could be spent elsewhere. So be courteous and respectful and remember that no member of the Revellers owes you a Teleport, Rez, Buff or use of their trade skill at cost. 
<br />

<br />
Honor and Respect: As a player without a guild you are responsible only to yourself. If you choose to join The Revellers, then you take on the additional responsibility of defending the honor and building the respect of the guild. We don't expect you to become selfless and dedicate all your time to others, or spineless or to change your fundamental personality. Where possible however, if someone asks for help and you are able, please assist them. 
<br />
If there is a misunderstanding, even if you are in the right, please keep a level head and try to negotiate towards a solution. If someone is being unreasonable, do not sink to their level. If you cannot come to an understanding, either remove yourself from the situation or use /petition to ask for assistance. Civility and common courtesy are sorely lacking in many situations in EverQuest. Part of our mission is to promote and display a more respectful, cooperative attitude and atmosphere in Norrath, be that while you are hunting, questing, camping, or during guild events. 
<br />
Keep in mind that all of your individual actions reflect on the guild as a whole. We understand that there are difficult people and difficult situations that can occur on a daily basis. Please try to keep cool about it and feel free to ask for suggestions on how to handle such situations on guildchat. Many tense situations can be defused when dealt with in a calm, cool manner. If you feel they can't (and it does happen), don't resort to threats, insults, or vengeful behavior. Remove yourself from the situation or, if it's warranted, /petition or /report. Verant is far better equipped to weed out the truly bad folks than you, or The Revellers, are. 
<br />

<br />
Please do not ever conspire to get someone killed, either through intentional 'training', misinformation, or bug exploitation.
<br />
NOTE: If someone intentionally bites off more than they can chew, and then yells their bloody head off expecting you to join in, you are certainly under no obligation to assist them. By the same token, if someone intentionally bites off more than they can chew because you TOLD them you would help, they have every right to expect your assistance.
<br />

<br />
Please do not ever conspire to cheat or defraud another player of items or money.
<br />

<br />

<br />
Original charter by Kadzer Troublemaker.
<br />
Updated by Malken Gneebiter and Serenya Soulhealer</td>
